#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054540 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0ab12b8-b1c9-5192-91be-cebc968d9587" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Logarithm Without a Calculator Using the Change of Base Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "fc85eeb4-dbc0-5ea7-af3a-60270d6ae722" :question/math-academy-id "e-4089" :question/problem "Calculate $\\log_{16}(32)$ without using a calculator." :question/worked-solution "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n\\log_a X = \\dfrac {\\log_b X} {\\log_b a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=16$ and $X =32.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ are powers of $2,$ we set $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{16}⁡(32) & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(32)}{{log}_{2}⁡(16)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{5})}{{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054541 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054744 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87ee4eae-702f-59f0-aff4-46c9acb89f6c" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Logarithm Using the Change of Base Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "15844e53-9573-5e6f-8fef-debbe0a142ba" :question/math-academy-id "e-4091" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\log x ?$ \n\nI. $\\dfrac {\\log_{2} x} {\\log_{2} 10}$\n\nII. $\\dfrac {\\log_{2} 10} {\\log_{2} x}$\n\nIII. $\\log_{2}\\left(\\dfrac{x}{10}\\right)$" :question/worked-solution "The change of base formula for logarithms is\n\n$$\n\\log_a X = \\dfrac {\\log_b X} {\\log_b a}.\n$$\n\nThe change of base formula works with any new base. In this example, the choices are written using base $2,$ so we rewrite $\\log x$ in terms of $\\log_2.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡x & ={log}_{10}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{{log}_{2}⁡10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054543 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bccd26ff-1dc5-5817-962b-a1ef1f46b2fb" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Logarithm With a Calculator Using the Change of Base Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "890afebc-d130-5dbc-aaf7-c2cd4db193f6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4100" :question/problem "Use a calculator to evaluate $\\log_3 (7)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let's calculate $\\log_3 (7)$ by changing the base $3$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).\n\nWe use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n\\log_a X = \\dfrac {\\log_b X} {\\log_b a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=3,$ $X =7,$ and $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{3}⁡(7) & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(7)}{{log}_{10}⁡(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{0.845\\,10}{0.477\\,12} \\\\  & ≈1.77.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bccd26ff-1dc5-5817-962b-a1ef1f46b2fb" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Logarithm With a Calculator Using the Change of Base Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13b65618-43ee-532e-a839-a31e265d785c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.812" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522059} {:answer/id #uuid "180aac80-cd6c-553f-9390-bd5447a64e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.917" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522070} {:answer/id #uuid "202305ae-992e-5dff-bc4e-bc45335f1658" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.714" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522092} {:answer/id #uuid "6d30e107-e689-5ca8-ade5-ea5a816ad541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.893" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522241} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c52165-df02-5476-941b-b3846aa44552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.765" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13b65618-43ee-532e-a839-a31e265d785c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.812" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522059} :answer-field/id #uuid "e017985b-c529-50e2-9421-397fcbb26ef9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c277570-c608-5c8a-9eec-65493369dacb" :question/math-academy-id "q-108372" :question/problem "Use a calculator to evaluate ${log}_{11}⁡(7)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let's calculate ${log}_{11}⁡(7)$ by changing the base $11$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).\n\nWe use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=11,$ $X=7,$ $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{11}⁡(7) & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(7)}{{log}_{10}⁡(11)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{0.845\\,098}{1.041\\,393} \\\\  & ≈0.812\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522747 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054744 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87ee4eae-702f-59f0-aff4-46c9acb89f6c" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Logarithm Using the Change of Base Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f05b9105-6358-56c2-af8c-ebeaec8564d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f05b9105-6358-56c2-af8c-ebeaec8564d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522531} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5c30e83-ea24-50fa-94a2-e0cd96a4bf88" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "834c413e-3660-5a12-aa09-b30d7cd9a51f" :question/math-academy-id "q-262839" :question/problem "Let $\\operatorname{log}⁡x=t.$ Express ${log}_{1000}⁡x$ via the variable $t.$\n\n${log}_{1000}⁡x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nWe want to change from base $a=1000$ to base $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{1000}⁡x & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡x}{{log}_{10}⁡(1000)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the expression in the denominator using exponents, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡x}{{log}_{10}⁡(1000)} & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡x}{{log}_{10}⁡({10}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡x}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{log}⁡x=t,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n{log}_{1000}⁡x=\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡x}{3}=\\frac{t}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bccd26ff-1dc5-5817-962b-a1ef1f46b2fb" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Logarithm With a Calculator Using the Change of Base Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e53d2060-f4c9-588d-b716-6b6725d895f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.416" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e53d2060-f4c9-588d-b716-6b6725d895f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.416" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522509} :answer-field/id #uuid "99060676-2b65-517f-864d-a46840395897" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd36bb1c-2d38-5fe5-b95b-ae2bbaecd296" :question/math-academy-id "q-262883" :question/problem "Use a calculator to evaluate ${log}_{8}⁡(19)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\n${log}_{8}⁡(19)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's calculate ${log}_{8}⁡(19)$ by changing the base $8$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).\n\nWe use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=8,$ $X=19,$ $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{8}⁡(19) & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(19)}{{log}_{10}⁡(8)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(19)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(8)} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{1.278\\,754}{0.903\\,090} \\\\  & ≈1.416\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055183 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0ab12b8-b1c9-5192-91be-cebc968d9587" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Logarithm Without a Calculator Using the Change of Base Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca66def7-3c65-5210-99d9-f0db68c4888c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca66def7-3c65-5210-99d9-f0db68c4888c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522440} :answer-field/id #uuid "72fdab3a-5e80-5092-81a0-756921237d3c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ba35fd5-f0a2-573b-abd8-5bda612260aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-262884" :question/problem "Expressed as a fraction in its simplest form, ${log}_{16}⁡(64)$ equals{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=16$ and $X=64.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ are powers of $2,$ we set $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{16}⁡(64) & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(64)}{{log}_{2}⁡(16)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{6})}{{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522741 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054744 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87ee4eae-702f-59f0-aff4-46c9acb89f6c" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Logarithm Using the Change of Base Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42c12419-a232-5cd2-b235-39a6a1843fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42c12419-a232-5cd2-b235-39a6a1843fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522164} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc3e8381-6b4f-5e93-ae04-8cf9545b1218" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522653}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7501f09d-5828-597b-9243-c1ed53d4a63e" :question/math-academy-id "q-262939" :question/problem "If ${log}_{125}⁡x=\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{k},$ where $k$ is an integer, then $k=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nWe want to change from base $a=125$ to base $b=5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{125}⁡x & =\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{{log}_{5}⁡125}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the expression in the denominator using exponents, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{{log}_{5}⁡125} & =\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{{log}_{5}⁡({5}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{log}_{125}⁡x=\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{3}.\n$$\n\nHence, $k=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0ab12b8-b1c9-5192-91be-cebc968d9587" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Logarithm Without a Calculator Using the Change of Base Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96517480-c58a-580a-bd6c-7724f8c25364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054010} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f3604e-93c4-543c-85d4-015c8fe7e1ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054011} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d3f4da-921c-581d-b2f2-9c94396b9176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054012} {:answer/id #uuid "1bd17a35-4d96-574e-94c2-099f33db7738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054013} {:answer/id #uuid "2d69af09-12b4-5f14-a76b-d95e41ad99a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d69af09-12b4-5f14-a76b-d95e41ad99a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054014} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c9c30ac-745b-5ac6-8f1f-5c84b0f7083a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d4f6e3a6-36a7-5dcc-b176-d20ea50c924d" :question/math-academy-id "q-66882" :question/problem "${log}_{36}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{6})=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=36$ and $X=\\sqrt[3]{6}.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ can be presented as a power of $6,$ we set $b=6.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{36}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{6}) & =\\frac{{log}_{6}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{6})}{{log}_{6}⁡(36)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{6}⁡({6}^{1/3})}{{log}_{6}⁡({6}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
